							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6037#msg6037"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6037#msg6037">Re:You've got to be kidding me...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #10 on:</b> March 08, 2004, 10:29:09 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I see, so it&#039;s wrong to have an honor roll because some poor little losers might feel left off if they don&#039;t make it, but having athletic competitions is fine. &nbsp;How retarded. &nbsp;Those who are good are sports get far more attention in high school than the &quot;good scholars&quot;. &nbsp;heh... obviously. &nbsp;So getting cut from the sports team would be far more painful than not making the honor roll. &nbsp;Anyway, how did our school systems get filled up with a bunch of idiot, touchy feely, i&#039;m alright, you&#039;re alright, no competition, turn all the kids into total pansies - administrators? &nbsp;<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
