						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6060#msg6060"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=602.msg6060#msg6060">Re:You've got to be kidding me...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #12 on:</b> March 09, 2004, 12:22:21 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I agree!<br /><br />Good thing these people are not in charge of politics. &nbsp;Imagine having an election where we were afraid of making the losing candidates feel rejected?<br /><br />&quot;The new person to hold this office is now.... EVERYONE who ran! &nbsp;Yes, regardless of votes, everyone who ran for this public office now holds that position so that no one feel bad!&quot;<br />or<br />&quot;We are sorry to inform you that we cannot reveal the identity of the new president of the United States. &nbsp;Announcing that would undoubtedly affect the morale and psychological stability of the losing candidates or the actually winner his/herself...&quot;<br /><br />Or... we could do away with all Nobel Peace Prizes, the Olympics, Prom Queen and King, Person of the Year, Team Captain...<br /><br />Radicals make me sick :(
						</td>
					</tr>
